      <h2>The Parliamentary Briefing</h2>
      <p>
        The Parliamentary Launch of Healthier UK brought together parliamentarians from across all political parties, clinical leaders from the College of Medicine and British Society of Lifestyle Medicine, and leaders of regional combined authorities.
      </p>

      <img src="assets/images/parliamentary-reception.jpeg" alt="Healthier UK coalition members at the Parliamentary reception in Westminster" style="width:100%;">

      <h2>Core proposals presented to government</h2>
      <div class="policy-step">
        <div class="policy-step-number">1</div>
        <div class="policy-step-body">
          <h4>Cross-Government Mission Ownership</h4>
          <p>Framing health creation as a whole-of-government mission that cuts across Treasury, Housing, Transport, Environment, and Work &amp; Pensions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-step">
        <div class="policy-step-number">2</div>
        <div class="policy-step-body">
          <h4>Rebalancing Spending: Invest to Save</h4>
          <p>Factoring avoided future costs into spending reviews to enable meaningful financial shifts from acute crisis management into preventative community health.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-step">
        <div class="policy-step-number">3</div>
        <div class="policy-step-body">
          <h4>Permanent Operating Models for Mayors</h4>
          <p>Moving from short-term demonstrator pilots to multi-year devolved health creation funding for Mayoral Combined authorities.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

